// ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓
// ┃                    niri Configuration                       ┃
// ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛
// niri is the desktop session on this machine (Hyprland retired).
// Noctalia is the shell here: bar, launcher, notifications, OSDs,
// wallpaper, idle handling and the lock screen all come from it, so
// separate bar/notification/idle/wallpaper daemons are intentionally absent.
// https://niri-wm.github.io/niri/Configuration:-Introduction
//
// This file is machine-agnostic (niri/noctalia have no arch/platform-
// specific parts, x64 and Apple Silicon alike) and is meant to be
// identical on every machine. The one exception is host.kdl (included
// below), which carries the actual keyboard layout + monitor facts for
// whichever machine it's deployed on — see dotconfig/niri/hosts/ for the
// other known machines' versions of that file.

// Cursor theme + size for Wayland and Qt apps.
environment {
    XCURSOR_THEME "capitaine-cursors"
    XCURSOR_SIZE "24"
    QT_CURSOR_SIZE "24"
}

// Per-machine input (keyboard layout) + output (monitor) facts — the only
// genuinely machine-specific part of this config. See host.kdl and
// dotconfig/niri/hosts/ for other known machines.
include "host.kdl"

// No client-side decorations — niri draws its own borders/shadows below.
prefer-no-csd

layout {
    gaps 8

    // Don't recenter the focused column when it's already fully visible —
    // less view-jitter while navigating a wide scrollable row.
    center-focused-column "never"

    focus-ring {
        width 2
        active-gradient from="#82dccc" to="#01ccff" angle=90
        inactive-color "#182545"
    }

    border {
        off
    }

    shadow {
        on
        softness 30
        spread 3
        color "#00000066"
    }

    preset-column-widths {
        proportion 0.33333
        proportion 0.5
        proportion 0.66667
    }

    default-column-width { proportion 0.5; }
}

screenshot-path "~/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot from %Y-%m-%d %H-%M-%S.png"

// Noctalia is the shell: bar, tray, notifications, OSDs, wallpaper,
// idle/lock and network status all live here instead of separate daemons.
spawn-at-startup "noctalia" "--daemon"

// Polkit auth-agent: provided by noctalia's built-in agent
// (polkit_agent=true in noctalia settings) — no separate spawn needed.

// X11 app compatibility (niri has no built-in Xwayland).
// niri auto-spawns "xwayland-satellite" on the PATH if present — it's not
// installed yet, so X11-only apps won't work until you
// `sudo pacman -S xwayland-satellite` (confirmed via a nested test run:
// niri logs a graceful warning and disables the integration without it).

// Screen-share / ScreenCast portal: /usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/niri-portals.conf
// (shipped by the niri package) prefers the "gnome" backend, but it's not
// pulled in automatically — `sudo pacman -S xdg-desktop-portal-gnome` is
// required or screen-share (e.g. in browsers for Meet) silently fails, since
// xdg-desktop-portal-gtk (the fallback) doesn't implement ScreenCast. Pulls
// in nautilus/gtk4/libadwaita/gnome-desktop-4 as deps — confirmed against
// niri's own wiki that gnome is the only supported screencast backend
// (xdg-desktop-portal-wlr is not a substitute and can conflict if both are
// installed).

window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"firefox$"# title="^Picture-in-Picture$"
    open-floating true
}

window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^org\.pulseaudio\.pavucontrol$"#
    open-floating true
}

window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^blueman-manager$"#
    open-floating true
}

window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^(polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1|polkit-kde-authentication-agent-1|org\.kde\.polkit-kde-authentication-agent-1)$"#
    open-floating true
}

// Noctalia's Settings window (theme/palette picker lives here) — without
// this it tiles into the scrollable column layout instead of opening as
// a normal floating panel. app-id + sizing per Noctalia's own niri docs.
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^dev\.noctalia\.Noctalia$"#
    open-floating true
    default-column-width { fixed 1080; }
    default-window-height { fixed 920; }
}

window-rule {
    match title="^(Open File|Save File)$"
    open-floating true
}

window-rule {
    geometry-corner-radius 8
    clip-to-geometry true
}

hotkey-overlay {
    skip-at-startup
}

// Required per Noctalia's niri compositor docs — without it, window
// activation requests from Noctalia panels (settings, notifications,
// control-center) can be silently ignored.
debug {
    honor-xdg-activation-with-invalid-serial
}

binds {
    Mod+Shift+Slash { show-hotkey-overlay; }

    // ======= Application launchers =======
    Mod+Return hotkey-overlay-title="Open a Terminal: kitty" { spawn "kitty"; }
    Mod+E      hotkey-overlay-title="File Manager: dolphin"  { spawn "dolphin"; }
    Mod+Space  hotkey-overlay-title="App Launcher: Noctalia" { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "panel-open" "launcher"; }

    // Noctalia's own screenshot tooling (replaces grim/slurp/swappy).
    Mod+S       { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "screenshot-region"; }
    Mod+Shift+S { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "screenshot-fullscreen"; }

    // Noctalia session actions (lock / logout).
    Mod+L         hotkey-overlay-title="Lock the Screen" { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "session" "lock"; }
    Mod+Shift+M   hotkey-overlay-title="Log Out"         { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "session" "logout"; }

    // Control center / settings.
    Mod+O { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "panel-open" "control-center"; }

    // Full Settings window — theme mode lives in control-center above, but
    // the color palette picker (Appearance > Theme > Palette, including the
    // custom ones in dotconfig/noctalia/palettes/) only lives in here.
    Mod+Shift+O hotkey-overlay-title="Settings (theme / palette)" { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "settings-toggle"; }

    // ======= Volume / mic — routed through Noctalia so its OSD fires =======
    XF86AudioRaiseVolume allow-when-locked=true { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "volume-up"; }
    XF86AudioLowerVolume allow-when-locked=true { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "volume-down"; }
    XF86AudioMute         allow-when-locked=true { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "volume-mute"; }
    XF86AudioMicMute      allow-when-locked=true { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "mic-mute"; }

    // ======= Playback control =======
    XF86AudioPlay allow-when-locked=true { spawn "playerctl" "play-pause"; }
    XF86AudioNext allow-when-locked=true { spawn "playerctl" "next"; }
    XF86AudioPrev allow-when-locked=true { spawn "playerctl" "previous"; }

    // ======= Screen brightness — routed through Noctalia for its OSD =======
    XF86MonBrightnessUp   allow-when-locked=true { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "brightness-up"; }
    XF86MonBrightnessDown allow-when-locked=true { spawn "noctalia" "msg" "brightness-down"; }

    // ======= Window management (niri's scrollable-column defaults) =======
    Mod+Q repeat=false { close-window; }

    Mod+Left  { focus-column-left; }
    Mod+Down  { focus-window-down; }
    Mod+Up    { focus-window-up; }
    Mod+Right { focus-column-right; }

    // Vim-style duplicates of the above (Mod+L is already "Lock the
    // Screen" below, so there's no H/J/K/L full set — right stays arrow-only).
    Mod+H { focus-column-left; }
    Mod+J { focus-window-down; }
    Mod+K { focus-window-up; }

    Mod+Ctrl+Left  { move-column-left; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Down  { move-window-down; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Up    { move-window-up; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Right { move-column-right; }

    Mod+Home { focus-column-first; }
    Mod+End  { focus-column-last; }

    Mod+Shift+Left  { focus-monitor-left; }
    Mod+Shift+Down  { focus-monitor-down; }
    Mod+Shift+Up    { focus-monitor-up; }
    Mod+Shift+Right { focus-monitor-right; }

    // Send the focused window (not just the column) to another monitor.
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Left  { move-window-to-monitor-left; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Down  { move-window-to-monitor-down; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Up    { move-window-to-monitor-up; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Right { move-window-to-monitor-right; }

    Mod+Page_Down { focus-workspace-down; }
    Mod+Page_Up   { focus-workspace-up; }
    Mod+U         { focus-workspace-down; }
    Mod+I         { focus-workspace-up; }

    Mod+WheelScrollDown cooldown-ms=150 { focus-workspace-down; }
    Mod+WheelScrollUp   cooldown-ms=150 { focus-workspace-up; }

    Mod+1 { focus-workspace 1; }
    Mod+2 { focus-workspace 2; }
    Mod+3 { focus-workspace 3; }
    Mod+4 { focus-workspace 4; }
    Mod+5 { focus-workspace 5; }
    Mod+6 { focus-workspace 6; }
    Mod+7 { focus-workspace 7; }
    Mod+8 { focus-workspace 8; }
    Mod+9 { focus-workspace 9; }
    Mod+Ctrl+1 { move-column-to-workspace 1; }
    Mod+Ctrl+2 { move-column-to-workspace 2; }
    Mod+Ctrl+3 { move-column-to-workspace 3; }
    Mod+Ctrl+4 { move-column-to-workspace 4; }
    Mod+Ctrl+5 { move-column-to-workspace 5; }
    Mod+Ctrl+6 { move-column-to-workspace 6; }
    Mod+Ctrl+7 { move-column-to-workspace 7; }
    Mod+Ctrl+8 { move-column-to-workspace 8; }
    Mod+Ctrl+9 { move-column-to-workspace 9; }

    Mod+BracketLeft  { consume-or-expel-window-left; }
    Mod+BracketRight { consume-or-expel-window-right; }
    Mod+Comma        { consume-window-into-column; }
    Mod+Period       { expel-window-from-column; }

    Mod+R       { switch-preset-column-width; }
    Mod+Shift+R { switch-preset-column-width-back; }

    Mod+F       { maximize-column; }
    Mod+Shift+F { fullscreen-window; }
    Mod+V       { toggle-window-floating; }
    Mod+Shift+V { switch-focus-between-floating-and-tiling; }
    Mod+W       { toggle-column-tabbed-display; }
    Mod+C       { center-column; }

    Mod+Minus { set-column-width "-10%"; }
    Mod+Equal { set-column-width "+10%"; }

    Print       { screenshot-screen; }
    Alt+Print   { screenshot-window; }

    Mod+Escape allow-inhibiting=false { toggle-keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit; }

    Mod+Shift+E     { quit; }
    Ctrl+Alt+Delete { quit; }
    Mod+Shift+P     { power-off-monitors; }
}
